# Keystores

Android release keys for this project. Jenkins reads them by **package
name** (`applicationIdentifier` in Player Settings), so an AAB build needs
no Jenkins configuration at all - commit the key here and push.

```
Keystores/
  com.pearz.meowpuzzle.keystore
  com.pearz.meowpuzzle.properties
```

`<package>.properties`:

```
storePass=...
alias=pearz
aliasPass=...
```

- `.jks` works as well as `.keystore`.
- `aliasPass` may be omitted when the alias uses the store password.
- Lookup order is `<applicationIdentifier>`, then the product name without
  spaces, then `default`.

Create the key once (back it up - losing it means the app can never be
updated on Google Play again):

```
keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore Keystores/com.pearz.meowpuzzle.keystore \
  -alias pearz -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
```

## Before you commit

The passwords in `.properties` are plain text. Anyone who can read this
repository can sign a build as you, so this folder belongs in a **private**
repository only.

If the key must not be in git, leave the `.properties` file out and set
`UMP_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASS`, `UMP_ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS` and
`UMP_ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS_PASS` as Jenkins credentials instead, or keep the
whole entry in `~/.pearz/keystores` on the build machine.
